# DAMMWT agent workflow

## Plan first

For non-trivial work, plan before implementing. If scope or approach is ambiguous, ask 1–2 critical clarifying questions, then proceed.

## Orchestrate + parallel subagents

Default to planning/orchestration. Fan out independent workstreams to multiple parallel subagents (e.g. assets vs web vs Electron vs verify). Do not run long serial solo loops when streams are independent.

## Rebuild Electron after every pass (hard habit)

After each meaningful pass that touches Electron, renderer, media, seed, or IPC:

1. Prefer `npm run review:electron` (rebuilds native ABI, builds, launches, brings window forward on macOS).
2. Or manually: `npx @electron/rebuild -f -w better-sqlite3` if ABI issues, then `npm start` (or `npm run dev`).
3. Bring the app window forward when possible so Dave can review immediately.

Do not skip relaunch “until the end” when the pass affected the desktop app.

## Branch context

Review tip often lands on gallery/media feature branches (e.g. `cursor/gallery-file-links-c55d`). Do not assume `main`; check `git branch --show-current` and work on the active review branch.
